  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "40E+DGVchDh9hVEo+ixPINjH/dk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:32.452Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Two facts combine into one conclusion. Camunda 7 Community reached its final feature release on 14 October 2025, after which *\"the repository will be archived shortly after. After this date, no further releases, including security patches, will be made\"* \u2014 and the GitHub API confirms `archived: true`. Enterprise received an extension to 2030; Community did not.\n\nCamunda 8's licence grants use *\"only and limited to the Use in or for the purpose of Using the Software in Non-Production Environment\"*, defined to exclude *\"any live or production systems\"*, with the alternative stated bluntly: *\"You must purchase a commercial license ... or You must refrain from Using the Software.\"* The key may not be *\"move[d], change[d], disable[d], or circumvent[ed]\"*.\n\nSo the only Apache-2.0 Camunda is unpatched abandonware and the only maintained Camunda is production-forbidden without payment. For a buyer under BSI or NIS2 obligations each is disqualifying in a different way. Note the asymmetry that survives: the Exporter API \u2014 the natural integration seam \u2014 is Apache-2.0, while the engine it exports from is not.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:32.452846Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:32.452850Z"
    }
  },
